  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="319254f6-8187-5a87-8d1a-eef42f242f1f" activityNameId="42918311-e84c-5286-969e-09e6d4a9ac58" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, production mix photovoltaic, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, production mix photovoltaic, at plant
Annual output of grid-connected PV power plants differentiated for roof-top, facade and centralized power plants. Technology and installation type breakdown based on literature (IEA-PVPS Task 1 and Fraunhofer ISE reports) and expert estimates. Average yield based on national statistics (Swissolar annual reports 2012-2018). The lifetime of PV systems is estimated at 30 years and a linear degradation rate of 0.7% per year is assumed (10.5% on average over 30 years) based on the PEFCR PV electricity.\nTechnology: Electricity production with grid-connected photovoltaic power plants.\nTime period: Time of publications\nVersion: 1\nEnergy values: Undefined\n100.0\nProduction volume: Total PV electricity production in 2018: approximately 2000 TWh in Switzerland.\nLocal category: Photovoltaik\nLocal subcategory: Kraftwerke\nUVEK 2022 source file:174-photovoltaics-global-supply-chain-v2.5._X-elec-CH.xml\n\n
UUID: d2ecb765-db25-37a5-b678-26606f6e2cf1
Production mix of photovoltaic electricity in the country. Annual output, Roof-Top: 976, Annual output, Facade: 683 kWh/kWp, Annual output, centralized PV systems: 1040 kWh/kWp. Amount of solar energy transformed to electricity. Waste heat emission due to losses of electricity in the system.
Location: undefined
Technology: Electricity production with grid-connected photovoltaic power plants.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: Total PV electricity production in 2018: approximately 2000 TWh in Switzerland.
Sampling: Statistical data for CH. 
Extrapolations: Water demand estimated at 20 L per m2 PV module over life time of the system.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d2ecb765-db25-37a5-b678-26606f6e2cf1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
